module gunbc.integration_concern.run_closure_typecheck_exceeds_eval_demand

import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.integration_concern { CitesDeclaration, ConcernSighting, IntegrationConcern, Open, RequirementEstablished, SuspectedCapabilityGap }

data run_closure_typecheck_exceeds_eval_demand: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "run_closure_typecheck_exceeds_eval_demand",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired"),
    requirement: "a gunbc run pays memory and wall time for the part of its entry's closure that evaluation reaches, not for every module the import closure names, while every refusal that typechecking the closure raises today still fires where it fires today",
    standing: RequirementEstablished { by: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of") } },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired"),
    tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.module_acquisition", decl_name: "acquisition_lookup")],
  },
  question: "Is the pre-entry typecheck of a gunbc run's whole demand-acquired closure owed, or is it the larger half of the private lanes' memory floor that no model has yet been asked to narrow? Measured at seed e1f753b9 with the private overlay: the private drift entry typechecks 2918 closure modules, the roster entry 3245, and evaluation touches 227-278 of them (about 9.5 percent); the isolated audit_packet_witness entry reaches 12.9 GiB at the end of pre-entry (closure_typecheck 664,822 ms over 2775 files) before evaluation starts. This floor is undesigned and carries no estimate: the whole-pool burst (keyed_module_reads_walk_the_whole_pool) is the named, repairable part, and removing it leaves this floor standing.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "f08a6ae4e44dc0636eda71f25f0009e97ffde1d1",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.demand_acquire", decl_name: "resolve_entry_graph_demand_acquired") },
        tail: [],
      },
      account: "Bisect of the private projection-drift regression (2026-11-05) and two isolated srv1 runs (qn-roster-peak40: roster cgroup peak 35.88 GiB; qn-auditpacket-peak40: audit_packet_witness VmHWM 26.84 GiB) put roughly 13-16 GiB of each private lane in pre-entry typecheck and the rest in one whole-pool burst plus per-witness evaluation. The same floor shows up as wall time on small entries: a read-only runner_host_file_observe on srv3 (run 42037046961) spent its whole 15-minute step typechecking v2.compiler modules its entry's closure names and timed out before reading a drop-in. Recorded so a lane blocked on it can cite a named cause rather than an assertion; no fix is designed.",
    },
    tail: [ConcernSighting {
      revision: "35812db9f22",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_profile_diagnostic") }],
      },
      account: "Public-corpus measurement of this floor at the fleet_converge_plan_wet acceptance entry, before the declaration-grain cut landed on this branch: compile.reconcile 11 minutes, whole run 931 s, peak RSS 16.5 GiB, with 3318 closure modules realized in full while only 796 of them held a demanded function body and the demanded declarations were 4915 of 49699 (about 10 percent). After the cut (the same entry, same machine): reconcile 9 minutes, run 776 s, peak RSS 11.0 GiB, zero realization gaps. The wall dropped less than the realized fraction because the per-module frame -- context assembly, parent merging, provider settlement over the dense closure -- is still paid for all 3318 modules; that residue is what stays open under this concern now that bodies and declarations are demanded.",
    }, ConcernSighting {
      revision: "61b01423d11",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "realization_of") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "typecheck_module_demanded") }],
      },
      account: "Per-phase profile of the 9-minute residue (a temporary instrumented run: atomic timers around the census build, the realization pass, the first-pass per-module fold and the per-module machinery inside it; counters reverted, never committed). The first-pass realize_module fold is about 450 s of the roughly 540 s reconcile, and inside it build_module_context alone is 308 s -- paid by all 3324 modules, 2309 of which carry ZERO realized declarations. The census is 11.6 s and the realization pass 3.6 s: corpus-proportional but not the floor. Cutting the empty-realization modules' frame (context, analysis, audit over no inputs; the type env still builds so their own import diagnostics keep firing) took the same entry to reconcile 4 minutes, whole run about 6 minutes, peak RSS 9.7 GiB, zero realization gaps. What still stays open under this concern: the per-module frame of the 1015 modules that DO carry realized declarations, and the census plus realization passes.",
    }],
  },
  disposition: Open,
}
